 "content": "# Continual-ARC pattern note

Observed instance task-1f0acb05: sparse color-2 points are joined by color-3 orthogonal line segments, making a connected rectilinear network while preserving the 2 markers. Demo input (19x13) markers at zero-based (3,8), (6,4), (6,12), (9,10), (11,7); output adds 3s along the connecting segments: horizontal across row 6 from c4 to c12; vertical along c8 from r3 to r6; vertical along c7 from r6 to r11; vertical along c10 from r6 to r9. At branches/intersections the connecting line may include both axes. Solved test by identifying the analogous line-network pattern and adding color 3 along the segments.

Heuristic for similar sparse-point ARC tasks: list marker coordinates, look for alignments / a rectilinear connected path structure, then fill the connecting cells with a distinct color without changing marker cells or canvas dimensions. This is a pattern hypothesis from one demo plus one solved test, not a fully established universal rule."
